<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · movement</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pietism</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pietists</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pietism was a movement of renewal within German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutheranism">Lutheranism</a> in the late 17th and 18th centuries, stressing personal faith, Bible study in small groups and practical charity. It was launched by Philipp Jakob Spener and developed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-halle">University of Halle</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/august-hermann-francke">August Hermann Francke</a>, whose orphanage and schools became a model. It influenced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravian-church">Moravian Church</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/methodism">Methodism</a> and education across northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p></div>
